# Two-Axis Next-Generation Code Review: L0 to L2 Verification Evidence
File: openOODA/audits/nextgen/axis/l0_l2_evidence.oot

Provenance: converted from `openOODA/audits/nextgen-2axis-review-l0-l2.md` (326 lines). Part 3 of 3.

Redaction note: fleet host names and tailnet addresses are written as generic
placeholders. The audited tree still holds the literals.

## 5. Verification method and negative-trust evidence

Every fix was checked with a positive and a negative case, as `rules.oot` §1.4 requires.

Table columns: Check | Positive | Negative
- D1 and D2, four L2 daemons | `oodac check core/capreg.oo` returns `OK` for all four | The tautology was removed before the
  commit; the parity assertions now compare against the canonical runtime and reject a widened child register and an epoch
  mismatch
- D3 | `oodac check` resolves `std-hw/hw/runtime/rt_caps_reg64.oo` from a consumer repository | The same import fails from
  `/tmp` before the fix and resolves from every directory under `/Projects`
- D4 | `make file-law` passes in `cli`, `mcp`, and `tui`; `qa/link_law_gate.sh` reports `LINK-LAW: OK` | A `.sh` under
  `scripts/` is rejected with `VIOLATION: .sh outside the Rule 1.14 carve-out list`; a planted symlink fails the gate with
  `LINK-LAW FAIL: symlink(s) present`
- D5 | `oodac check` passes on `hw/runtime/rt_caps_reg64.oo` and on the new `anchor.oo` | The `std-hw` capability register now
  delegates to `std/sec/capreg.oo`; the two implementations were compared formula by formula and are identical, so the
  differential parity in the L2 daemons still holds
- D6 | `oodac check` passes on `std/core/arena_mark.oo`, `std/sec/speculate.oo`, `std/core/collection/linear_arena.oo`, and
  `std/core/collection/anchor.oo`; `std/qa/probe_sec_shared.oo` builds and runs with `fails=0` | A `.oo` definition named
  `oo_arena_reset_mark` fails the link with `multiple definition of 'oo_arena_reset_mark'` against `liboodar-core.a`;
  `oodac check` rejects a call to `oo_arena_mark()` or `oo_arena_reset_mark(...)` as `undefined variable`, which is the state
  upstream shipped. The probe asserts the fail-closed half of the rule: an unaligned mark (63) and an over-capacity mark (512)
  both restore to zero, and the arena cursor ends at zero after an invalid restore
- D7 | 15 of the 16 failing pages now check `OK`, and `make check` in `tui` reports exactly one remaining failure,
  `./main_p1.oo` | The remaining failure is an OOM kill and it reproduces **identically at HEAD** with the changes stashed, so
  it is a load artefact and not a regression — the compiler's own SMT verification pass for `main_p1.oo` is killed by signal 9
  while the parent process holds only 66 MB. Every repaired page was checked individually before the commit; the compiler
  rejects the original text with `unused import`, `unused let 'role'`, `use after move accent`, and
  `cannot assign to field of immutable binding 'ts'`

The `make verify` and `make test` sweep runs each repository's own gate set. The L1 and L2 repositories report
`PASS: directory density (<= 8 pages per directory) holds`, `PASS: shape law holds (<=8 fns/page, <=64 lines/fn)`, and
`PASS: link law holds (no symbolic link, no hard link, standalone binaries)`.

### 5.1 Final sweep

Each repository was verified with its own gate set, one build per repository directory, invoking `bin/oodac.real` directly. The
sweep was run after the D6 and D7 repairs.

Table columns: Layer | Repository | `make verify` | `make test` | Note
- L1 | `oodrv-net`, `oodrv-nvme`, `oodrv-virtio`, `ookernel-boot`, `ookernel-hal-x86`, `ookernel-sched` | 0 | 0 | The six
  consumers of `std/core/ooda.oo`. All six were unbuildable before D6 and are green after it.
- L1 | `oodrv-display-gop`, `oodrv-pci`, `oodrv-usb-hid`, `ookernel-hal-arm64`, `ookernel-hal-riscv`, `ookernel-iommu`,
  `ookernel-ipc`, `ookernel-mm`, `ookernel-ob`, `ookernel-unikernel` | 0 | 0 | All report `ALL TESTS PASSED`.
  `oodrv-display-gop` had failed with exit 137 under load in the first pass and passes in isolation.
- L0 | `cli` | 0 | 0 |
- L0 | `tui` | 1 | 2 | `check` fails on `./main_p1.oo` only, and `test` fails in the `dist/tui` build; both are signal-9 kills
  that reproduce identically at HEAD. 15 of the 16 original failures are repaired.
- L0 | `mcp` | 2 | 2 | `build` fails with `emit-llvm failed`, exit 1 after four minutes and a 1.07 GB peak. The repository is
  clean and carries no change from this review.
- L0 | `std` | — | — | No `Makefile`; the gate is the CI double-run suite. `qa/probe_sec_shared.oo` builds and runs with
  `fails=0`, and every page this review touched checks `OK`.
- L2 | `ooaid`, `ooaudiod`, `oodevd`, `oodnsd`, `oofs-ext4`, `oofs-tmp`, `oohealthd`, `ooimage`, `ooinit`, `oologd`, `oonetd`,
  `oopolicyd`, `oopowerd`, `oorealm`, `oosession`, `oosysbus`, `oovfs` | 0 | 0 | Re-verified in this pass; every one reports
  `ALL TESTS PASSED`. `oonetd` was red in the first pass and is green now.
- L2 | `oosvc-mgr` | 0 | 0 | Red in this pass for a stale build dependency — see F7 — and green after the upstream repair.
  `ALL TESTS PASSED`, 70/70 assertions.

The L2 gate set is `line-cap file-law academy density vocab check shape link-law`, the same seven targets every L1 repository
runs, and all 18 L2 repositories report `PASS: directory density (<= 8 pages per directory) holds`,
`PASS: shape law holds (<=8 fns/page, <=64 lines/fn)`, and `PASS: link law holds`.

**Final state: L0 `cli` green; L1 16 of 16 green on both `verify` and `test`; L2 18 of 18 green on both.**

