## 6. Environment notes

The workspace runs concurrent review agents. Three observations follow from that and are recorded so the results are read
correctly.

1. **The compiler wrapper enforces a 240-second timeout per invocation and a two-slot concurrency limit.** Under this load a
   build that shares a repository with another agent serialises on the per-repo lock and is killed with `Error 124`. The
   verification sweep therefore invokes `bin/oodac.real` directly and runs one build per repository directory. A `Killed` or
   `Error 124` line in this environment is a resource artefact, not a test failure, and was re-run before any result was
   recorded.
2. **A from-source rebuild of the compiler was attempted and did not finish.**
   `bootstrap/oodac_pure_build main.oo /tmp/oodac-rebuild` reached `pure_build: check host=… nmods=375 timeout=3600s` and then
   stopped with `ERR_CHECK_TIMEOUT`. The host check of 375 modules did not complete within the limit under this load. The source
   and binary agreement for D3 rests on the resolver behaviour measurements in section 5, not on a completed rebuild.
3. **Concurrent work in `openOODA-core/oodac` and `openOODA-kernel/ookernel-ob` was left untouched.** The `oodac` commit in this
   review stage only `ast/load_import_parse.oo`; the wrapper and the untracked ELF in `bin/` belong to another agent and were
   deliberately not committed here. The `ookernel-ob` working tree was reverted by its owner during this review, so no change
   was made in that repository.
4. **Two remaining red results are load artefacts, and both were proven so by comparison against the unmodified tree.**
   `tui/main_p1.oo` is killed by signal 9 during `oodac check` — re-running the same check with the review changes stashed
   produces the identical kill, so the page is heavy rather than broken. `openOODA-core/mcp` fails its `build` target with
   `emit-llvm failed` and an exit status of 1 after four minutes and a 1.07 GB peak, and the `mcp` repository carries no
   uncommitted change; its `file-law` target, the only target this review touched, passes. Neither result was recorded as a
   pass.

